{"seq":4,"slug":"restorative-practices","title":"恢复性实践","docCount":3,"url":"/h/negotiation-communication/conflict-resolution/restorative-practices","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"restorative-justice","title":"恢复性正义 Restorative Justice","url":"/h/negotiation-communication/conflict-resolution/restorative-practices/restorative-justice","wordCount":3523,"readingTime":15},{"seq":2,"slug":"dialogue-circles","title":"对话圈与和平圈 Dialogue Circles and Peacemaking Circles","url":"/h/negotiation-communication/conflict-resolution/restorative-practices/dialogue-circles","wordCount":3400,"readingTime":14},{"seq":3,"slug":"post-conflict-reconstruction","title":"冲突后重建 Post-conflict Reconstruction","url":"/h/negotiation-communication/conflict-resolution/restorative-practices/post-conflict-reconstruction","wordCount":3595,"readingTime":15}],"introMarkdown":"# 恢复性实践\n\n恢复性实践代表了冲突处理领域的范式转换——从「谁对谁错」的归责逻辑转向「如何修复伤害、重建关系」的修复逻辑。这一理念源自恢复性正义运动，如今已广泛应用于学校、社区、企业和国际和平建设等多个领域。\n\n本章探讨恢复性正义的核心理念和实践框架、对话圈与和平圈的具体操作方法，以及冲突后重建信任和关系的系统策略。恢复性实践不是对传统冲突解决方法的否定，而是一种重要的补充——它特别适用于关系持续性强、信任修复价值高的场景。\n"}